WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:06.460
Dr. Bright, Dr. Clef, and Dr. Gears all sat
around a conference table, the monitor beside

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:13.100
them giving a direct encrypted video link
to O5-1, the most senior member of the legendary

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.070
O5 Council.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:20.920
Only one topic was on the roster today: The
inherent nature of one of their most problematic

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.590
anomalies, SCP-682, the Hard to Destroy Reptile.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:30.769
There were certain facts that were easy to
ascertain about SCP-682, like the fact that

00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:35.670
its default state appears to be vaguely reptilian,
the fact that it’s highly aggressive, and

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:39.570
the fact that it is seemingly impossible to
kill.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:43.320
The rest, it seems, is still largely shrouded
in mystery.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:48.320
“How can we expect to terminate this creature
if we don’t fully resolve to understand

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:49.320
it?”

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.320
Dr. Gears offered.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.109
“It appears that all of our efforts so far
have amounted to firing a gun in the dark

00:00:54.109 --> 00:00:55.670
and hoping for the best.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:00.129
Do you all have any idea how much money we’ve
blown on the termination effort so far?

00:01:00.129 --> 00:01:02.100
Believe me, the numbers would shock you.”

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:06.409
Dr. Bright chimed in with, “As the only
one in this room who’s literally been inside

00:01:06.409 --> 00:01:10.940
this monster’s head” - referring to the
incident wherein SCP-682 was made to ingest

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.880
Dr. Bright’s medallion in hopes of letting
the Doctor’s consciousness take over the

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.450
beast, which didn’t work - “I think I
speak with a degree of authority when I say

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:22.990
I’m not sure if we’d have any luck actually
understanding it.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:25.880
It’s like asking a volcano how it feels
about erupting.”

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.880
Dr. Clef’s thoughts on the matter were predictable.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:33.110
“Okay, look, I may not have mind-melded
with this abomination like Jack, but I’ve

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:36.200
got two working eyes and a decent brain attached
to them.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.840
That’s all I need to tell you our solution
here is obvious: More firepower.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:44.159
We’ve been going easy on this thing so far,
letting it face different anomalies one at

00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:49.340
a time, not going at it with any truly heavy
weaponry, and for some stupid reason, ruling

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:51.259
out nuclear armaments—“

00:01:51.259 --> 00:01:53.860
That had everyone around the room rolling
their eyes.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.299
“There he goes with the nukes again,”
Dr. Bright said.

00:01:57.299 --> 00:01:58.439
“Nukes, nukes, nukes.

00:01:58.439 --> 00:02:02.549
If you love nukes so much, why don’t you
marry them, eh, Clef?”

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:04.010
Clef grumbled in frustration.

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:06.789
“When did everyone around here get so risk-averse?

00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:10.759
Faint heart never won fair maid, or killed
giant ugly lizards!

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:13.570
Why should we treat nuke like it’s such
a dirty word?”

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:14.890
Dr. Gears sighed.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:19.760
“If the break room coffee machine malfunctioned,
you’d tell us to make sure the nuclear response

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:22.319
option stays on the table, Clef.”

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:24.180
Clef banged his hand on the table.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:27.480
“Because I believe in getting results, no
matter what!”

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.480
“ENOUGH!”

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.660
O5-1 barked, silencing the room.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:36.319
Everyone turned to the monitor and gave their
undivided attention as their superior spoke.

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:41.950
“I can staunchly confirm that we will not
be pursuing a nuclear option for 682 under

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.250
any circumstances.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:47.420
I don’t intend on creating a Godzilla we
need to fight.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.610
Gears, I think you’re on to something.

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:55.950
We’ve done all we can to analyze SCP-682
through the eyes of scientific empiricist,

00:02:55.950 --> 00:03:00.010
perhaps we need to look at it through the
eyes of its fellow anomalies - The ones that

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:01.739
aren’t completely insane, anyway.

00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:03.459
Make it happen, gentlemen.

00:03:03.459 --> 00:03:04.459
Chop chop.”

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:05.769
And so they did.

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:11.630
All three of the incredibly different doctors
did see the wisdom in O5-1’s new theory:

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:16.409
Perhaps they could gain a more holistic understanding
of SCP-682 by collating knowledge gained from

00:03:16.409 --> 00:03:18.040
other anomalies.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:22.420
And through this knowledge, they might also
be able to find a weakness that somehow slipped

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:23.650
by unnoticed.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:27.549
Right now, SCP-682 was like an impenetrable
locked door.

00:03:27.549 --> 00:03:31.910
But even the most durable locked door can
be defeated with the right key.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:37.069
There were certain anomalous perspectives
on SCP-682 that they already had.

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:44.159
Take, for example, that of SCP-343, the kindly
reality warper also known as God.

00:03:44.159 --> 00:03:49.739
When confronted with SCP-682 during a termination
attempt, the two of them seemed patently unaware

00:03:49.739 --> 00:03:51.849
of each other’s presence.

00:03:51.849 --> 00:03:58.159
When quizzed on the subject, 343 claimed that
682 wasn’t one of his, perhaps implying

00:03:58.159 --> 00:04:00.349
some kind of extradimensional origin.

00:04:00.349 --> 00:04:05.200
It also lends credence to the popular theory
that SCP-682 is one of the children of the

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:10.799
Scarlet King, though for now, that would still
remain nothing more than a theory, not something

00:04:10.799 --> 00:04:12.650
they could really act upon.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:18.479
This was why each of the three researchers,
following the orders from O5-1, began canvasing

00:04:18.479 --> 00:04:24.000
reactions from other intelligent anomalies,
in hopes of getting a useful kernel of information

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.660
from a fresh new angle.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:31.630
Dr. Bright, who has frankly seen far too many
movies, thought of himself as Clarice Starling,

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:36.340
interviewing a whole collection of Hannibal
Lecters in hopes of gaining a unique insight

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.509
that would help him catch the killer.

00:04:38.509 --> 00:04:43.259
When he shared this thought with Dr. Clef
and Dr. Gears, Gears told Bright that he didn’t

00:04:43.259 --> 00:04:46.430
watch movies, and Clef called Bright a nerd.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:50.580
After the proper safety precautions were put
in to make sure that the two never actually

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:57.639
came into physical or mental contact, Dr.
Clef had SCP-035 - the devious, diabolical

00:04:57.639 --> 00:05:03.130
Possessive Mask - attached to a mannequin
host body and brought in to observe SCP-682

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:05.710
in a sealed chamber.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:10.470
Clef asked the Possessive Mask to relay any
thoughts he had while looking at the beast.

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:15.160
Admittedly, Dr. Clef felt a little unnerved
by how gleeful the Mask looked while watching

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:18.980
the Hard to Destroy Reptile clambering around
its tank.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:25.660
“Oh yes, yes,” the Possessive Mask said,
its words like cyanide in the ears.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:29.400
“What a truly marvelous creature.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:34.060
So large, so powerful, so violent.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:37.740
I can feel the hatred radiating off of it
from here.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:41.669
You know, the hateful ones are often the easiest
to manipulate.

00:05:41.669 --> 00:05:47.070
There’s so much they’ll do for power,
so much they’ll sign away, while their malice

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.070
blinds them.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.070
Oh, delightful.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:50.340
Such a wonderful thought.

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:54.650
I don’t suppose you’d let him wear me,
would you?”

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:56.500
Dr. Clef shook his head.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.100
“Not on your life, creep.”

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:02.070
Sadly, it didn’t seem as though any new
insights had really been gained here.

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:05.949
Hopefully, Dr. Gears would have a little more
luck with his project.

00:06:05.949 --> 00:06:11.330
Dr. Gears had decided to take a more measured
approach - unsurprising, given this is Dr.

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:16.390
Gears we’re talking about - and went for
an intelligent anomaly who probably wasn’t

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:22.699
harboring some evil ulterior motive: SCP-507,
the Reluctant Dimension Hopper.

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:25.710
Two things highly benefited Dr. Gears in this
regard.

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:30.259
Firstly, the Reluctant Dimension Hopper had
gotten around and seen more things than pretty

00:06:30.259 --> 00:06:32.900
much any other mortal being in existence.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:40.419
Secondly, SCP-507 had certain aspirations
- Namely, to become an SCP Foundation researcher,

00:06:40.419 --> 00:06:45.300
where he could be accepted and make a profession
out of his interest in the supernatural.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.069
Gears could leverage this to gain cooperation.

00:06:48.069 --> 00:06:54.560
When SCP-507 was brought in to observe 682,
Gears noticed a certain flicker of recognition

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:58.800
in the Dimension Hopper’s eyes, before the
man opened his mouth and said, “Oh god,

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.539
not another one of those things.”

00:07:00.539 --> 00:07:02.360
Gears immediately fired back.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:04.720
“Another one, you say?”

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:05.900
SCP-507 nodded.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:10.270
“Yeah, during one of my jumps, I was in
this big, weird landscape covered in freaky-looking

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:11.270
rocks.

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:14.680
There were a whole bunch of these guys there,
like a herd or a pack or something.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.449
As soon as they saw me, they started chasing
me.

00:07:16.449 --> 00:07:19.701
It was honestly pretty tense, for a second
there, I didn’t even know if I’d make

00:07:19.701 --> 00:07:20.759
it out alive.”

00:07:20.759 --> 00:07:23.120
Dr. Gears nodded and continued taking notes.

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:27.120
“Do you have any further observations from
your time seeing these creatures in another

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.229
dimension?”

00:07:28.229 --> 00:07:32.819
SCP-507 shook his head, presumably disappointed
that he couldn’t offer more.

00:07:32.819 --> 00:07:37.020
“Thank you, that will be all then, 507,”
Dr. Gears said.

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:39.199
And, of course, that left one more.

00:07:39.199 --> 00:07:40.340
The maverick.

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:41.849
The joker in the pack.

00:07:41.849 --> 00:07:47.130
Dr. Jack Bright, the man from whom you can
only ever really expect the unexpected.

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:54.160
He’d decided to take the middle ground between
the offerings of Dr. Gears and Dr. Clef: SCP-049,

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:59.009
the Plague Doctor, the mysterious being who
can kill with a touch, but has aspirations

00:07:59.009 --> 00:08:00.009
to heal.

00:08:00.009 --> 00:08:05.540
Dr. Bright was extremely interested in seeing
what he had to say about the nasty reptile.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:10.230
That same day, the Plague Doctor was feeling
a little irritated, to say the least.

00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:14.900
He’d been conducting some extremely important
research into the Pestilence on a cow carcass

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:20.270
when suddenly, an order from the top deemed
he would no longer have access to animal subjects.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:24.710
Lavender had been pumped into his cell to
pacify him while five heavily-armored guards

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:27.479
entered and dragged out his latest subjects.

00:08:27.479 --> 00:08:31.400
It was cruel, it was inhumane, it was anti-science!

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:34.419
First, they’d taken away his live human
subjects.

00:08:34.419 --> 00:08:39.370
Then, they’d taken away his dead human subjects,
followed by his live animal subjects.

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:44.290
If he wasn’t even allowed to perform his
vital research on animal carcasses now, then

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.649
what hope did he have of making progress?

00:08:46.649 --> 00:08:51.380
While out there in the world, every single
day, the Pestilence spreads further.

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:54.240
Who even knows what form it has taken on now?

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:59.120
After all, diseases shift and mutate with
the times, and the whole world was a Petri

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:00.300
dish out there.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:04.420
As the Plague Doctor was lost in his musings,
Dr. Bright approached and rapped his knuckles

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:06.820
on the plexiglass of his containment chamber.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:09.680
“Leave me be, Doctor,” the Plague Doctor
sighed.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:13.120
“Haven’t you and your compatriots already
taken enough from me?”

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:17.480
“I’m not here to take, Doctor, I’m here
to give,” Dr. Bright said.

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:22.610
“I know we can be a little harsh in our
measures sometimes, Doc, but we’re cold,

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:23.610
not cruel.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:26.540
You play ball with us, you’ll find we can
be very amicable.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:30.230
To the tune of, say, getting your live animal
research privileges back?”

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:34.250
There was a moment of silence, before the
Plague Doctor rose up and walked over to the

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:36.740
divider between himself and Dr. Bright.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:40.460
He cocked his head slightly, as though taking
in Dr. Bright’s measure.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:43.360
“What would you have me do in return, Doctor?”

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:44.580
the Plague Doctor asked.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:45.770
Dr. Bright smiled.

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:48.350
“There’s just something I want you to
look at.”

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:53.260
With the assistance of a few security officers,
the Plague Doctor was moved over to an observation

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:56.870
chamber, joining onto a larger, more secure
chamber.

00:09:56.870 --> 00:10:02.440
The Plague Doctor sat on a plush chair, staring
through a one-way mirror into the larger chamber.

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:07.350
Dr. Bright turned on a dictaphone, hoping
to record any interesting observations the

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:08.820
Plague Doctor came out with.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:13.590
“What, pray tell, am I supposed to be looking
at, Dr. Bright?” he asked.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:14.610
“They’re bringing him in now.

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:16.550
Won’t be a moment,” Dr. Bright said.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:21.490
A large door in the larger chamber opened,
and several members of personnel dragged in

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:28.310
a tied-up, incapacitated SCP-682, looking
like it was still recovering from heavy injuries.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:31.649
Immediately, SCP-049 seemed to tense up.

00:10:31.649 --> 00:10:36.230
Dr. Bright was fascinated, watching the Plague
Doctor’s previously calm demeanor suddenly

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:39.230
become marred by clearly evident worry.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:40.630
What was he thinking?

00:10:40.630 --> 00:10:42.330
Would it be a useful insight?

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:46.639
The silence continued as the Plague Doctor
seemed to carefully observe the immobilized

00:10:46.639 --> 00:10:47.639
beast.

00:10:47.639 --> 00:10:52.839
For a moment or two, Dr. Bright even noticed
the Plague Doctor’s hands shaking slightly.

00:10:52.839 --> 00:10:56.269
Moments later, the Doctor cleared his throat
and said, “The Pestilence!

00:10:56.269 --> 00:10:58.070
Never have I seen it so malignant!”

00:10:58.070 --> 00:10:59.180
“Come again, Doc?”

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:00.180
Dr. Bright asked.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:01.180
“This...

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.180
Thing.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:03.529
It is sick, Doctor, dreadfully sick.

00:11:03.529 --> 00:11:08.910
It is a bastion of disease, a harbinger of
Plague, unlike anything that has ever been

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:09.910
seen before.

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:12.589
How long have you had this filthy thing within
your walls, Doctor?

00:11:12.589 --> 00:11:14.839
How many people have made contact with it?

00:11:14.839 --> 00:11:15.839
Quickly, please!

00:11:15.839 --> 00:11:17.890
I must know, for the safety of all of you!”

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:23.200
As the Plague Doctor became increasingly agitated,
Dr. Bright became a mix of deeply concerned

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:24.880
and incredibly curious.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:30.529
Sure, SCP-049 tended to go off about a lot
of things allegedly being infected with “The

00:11:30.529 --> 00:11:32.710
Pestilence”, but this is different.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:35.920
There is genuine fear shaking in the Plague
Doctor’s voice.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:41.110
“I feel unwell, Doctor,” the Plague Doctor
said, rising shakily to his feet.

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:42.970
“Please, escort me back to my chambers.

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:46.660
I simply cannot deal with such a case without
proper preparations.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.540
It would be too dangerous.”

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:52.560
Dr. Bright ordered the security personnel
to make the Plague Doctor’s desire a reality.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:57.170
He would be escorted back to his chamber,
be given a lavender supplement, as well as

00:11:57.170 --> 00:12:02.700
a meal of beef and hard cheese - his favorite-
to help him recuperate from his shock.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:07.709
But all throughout this process, Dr. Bright
had latched on to one fragment of the Doctor’s

00:12:07.709 --> 00:12:08.709
mutterings.

00:12:08.709 --> 00:12:13.170
“I simply cannot deal with such a case without
proper preparations.”

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:19.800
Did that mean, with the proper preparations,
SCP-049 could deal with SCP-682?

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:24.800
And as with most of 049’s “patients”,
did “deal” mean “kill?”

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:29.930
If so, then this project was really about
to bear some impressive fruit.

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:34.380
After giving the Plague Doctor a few days
to get himself reoriented, Dr. Bright returned

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:39.421
with another offer - One he wasn’t even
sure he had the authorization to make, but

00:12:39.421 --> 00:12:42.709
if his plan worked out, he was sure he could
swing it.

00:12:42.709 --> 00:12:46.630
He offered the Plague Doctor the chance to
work with human subjects again...

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:50.520
If he could first successfully treat SCP-682.

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:59.220
“It would certainly be an undertaking,”
SCP-049 said, trying to hide his clear discomfort.

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:02.699
“But for the sake of science, I must accept.”

00:13:02.699 --> 00:13:06.730
Over the next few days, the preparations were
drafted up, and the Plague Doctor was given

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:11.910
any equipment or resources he requested for
the task of “curing” SCP-682.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:18.320
Then, when the day came, SCP-682 was tied
up and sedated once again, and dragged into

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:23.410
a large cross-testing chamber where Dr. Bright,
the Plague Doctor, and several members of

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:25.250
security personnel were waiting.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:26.610
It was now or never.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.990
Would the Doctor be able to do it?

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:32.740
“For what it’s worth, I believe in you,
Doc,” Dr. Bright said, giving a tentative

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:33.760
thumbs up.

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:37.750
The Plague Doctor didn’t return the thumbs
up - he was too busy trying to stop himself

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:41.190
from visibly shaking in the face of this giant,
diseased monstrosity.

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:44.980
Would he have any hope of treating such a
beast?

00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:46.810
He exhaled and approached.

00:13:46.810 --> 00:13:50.860
As with all of his patients, his first step
would be to lay a hand on the monster, which

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:53.630
normally rendered it peaceful and still.

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:57.950
The Plague Doctor slowly walked over, his
hand extended, feeling the prickles of fear

00:13:57.950 --> 00:13:59.420
all over his body.

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:00.880
He could do this...

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:02.360
He could do this...

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:08.779
But as he approached, SCP-682 had somehow
freed one of its arms, and swung for SCP-682

00:14:08.779 --> 00:14:10.060
with its vicious claws.

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:15.670
049 screamed and stumbled back, hitting the
ground and crawling away in the opposite direction,

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:17.420
practically wheezing with terror.

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:21.970
He eventually gathered himself up into the
corner and curled into a ball, shaking.

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:27.980
Dr. Bright breathed a sigh of disappointment,
it seemed this entire venture had been a wash.

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:32.160
”Take 049 back to his cell,” Dr. Bright
said, resigned.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:33.660
“We’re all done here.”

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:37.829
For everyone else, it was just another failed
cross-test, quickly forgotten, with all the

00:14:37.829 --> 00:14:39.699
others.

00:14:39.699 --> 00:14:43.990
For SCP-049, it was one of the most traumatic
experiences of his life, one that would stay

00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:50.149
with him forever, and be the reason he would
always be afraid of SCP-682.

